# nr-exthost-worker-loop: the crate mixdog-exthost-worker (native/core/crates/mixdog-exthost-worker)

## native/core/Cargo.toml

1. [workspace] members: add after the line `    "crates/mixdog-exthost",`
       "crates/mixdog-exthost-worker",

2. [workspace.dependencies]: add after the line `mixdog-exthost = { path = "crates/mixdog-exthost" }`
       mixdog-exthost-worker = { path = "crates/mixdog-exthost-worker" }
   and, in the alphabetical block of the registry crates (before `libc`/after `crossbeam-*`, wherever `dunce` sorts)
       dunce = "1.0.5"
   (dunce 1.0.5 is already in Cargo.lock as a transitive dependency; the crate uses it for `realpathSync.native`'s path form.)

## native/core/Cargo.lock

Regenerate offline (`cargo metadata --offline --locked` will refuse; use `cargo update -w --offline`): a new package
`mixdog-exthost-worker` with dependencies bytes, dunce, libc, mixdog-workspace-hack, serde, serde_json, tokio, tokio-util,
windows-sys, and dev-dependencies mixdog-core-api, mixdog-exthost, mixdog-protocol, mixdog-rt, tempfile. No new external crate.

## native/core/crates/mixdog-workspace-hack/Cargo.toml

`cargo hakari generate` (the new crate has the hack line already). Nothing else.

## Dependency edges

None from an existing crate to the new one yet: the binary the pool starts in production is wired by the task that adds the
document methods (it replaces `node src/ext-host/worker.mjs` in ExtHostConfig.program/args). The new crate depends on no
workspace crate except mixdog-workspace-hack (dev-dependencies: mixdog-exthost, mixdog-core-api, mixdog-protocol, mixdog-rt).

## unify-test-features (D:\mixdog-build\tools\unify-test-features.py)

The new crate's dev-dependencies name no test-only feature except `mixdog-rt/test-support`; run the tool so the other crates' test
builds carry the same feature set.

## SERVICE_PENDING (compose_flip.rs)

Nothing to remove: the crate registers no protocol service.

## Registration in the worker binaries

`mixdog_exthost_worker::methods::register_document_methods(&mut Registry)` is empty; the tasks that port the document, office, pdf,
image and syntax methods fill it. The production worker's `main` (a bin of this crate, added by the first of those tasks) calls
`mixdog_exthost_worker::run::stdio()` first, then `serve(registry, input, output)` on a multi-thread runtime, and leaves through
`Runtime::shutdown_background` (see src/bin/ext_worker_dev.rs for the shape).
